/P 65 0 R
/S /Figure
/Alt (Image is a three-column table with the headers optical media, description, and storage capacity. There are 10 rows. The first three rows are types of CD drives all with a storage capacity of 700 MB. Row 1 is CD-ROM media, description is CD read-only memory media that is pre-recorded. Row 2 is CD-R media, description is CD recordable media that can be recorded one time. Row 3 is CD-RW media, description is CD rewritable media that can be recorded, erased, and re-recorded. The next four rows are types of DVD drives all with a storage capacity of 4.7 GB \(Single-Layer\)/8.5 GB \(Dual-Layer\). Row 4 is DVD-ROM media, decription is DVD read-only memory media that is pre-recorded. Row 5 is DVD-RAM media, description is DVD rewritable media that can be recorded, erased, and re-recorded. Row 6 is DVD+/-R media, description is DVD recordable media that can be recorded one time. Row 7 is DVD+/-RW media, description is DVD rewriteable media that can be recorded, erased, and re-recorded. The last three rows are types of BD drives all with a storage capacity of 25 GB \(Single-Layer\)/50 GB \(Dual-Layer\). Row 8 is BD-ROM media, description is Blu-ray recordable media that is pre-recorded with movies, games, or software. Row 9 is BD-R media, description is Blu-ray recordable media that can be recorded one time. Row 10 is BD-RE media, description is Blu-ray rewritable media that can be recorded, erased, and re-recorded.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [4]
/Pg 30 0 R
>>
